From 49b398c858fe856fd269ee8dc9f760b74b1d6f26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3350/3799] soh: rename func_800E64B0 ->
 AudioThread_SetChannelIo

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: queues an 0xFA command carrying three byte fields; which channel setting it drives is not established
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_thread.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_thread.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
index 64ef0582b..42aa22198 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
@@ -771,7 +771,8 @@ void AudioThread_ProcessChannelCmd(SequenceChannel* channel, AudioCmd* cmd) {
     }
 }
 
-void func_800E64B0(s32 arg0, s32 arg1, s32 arg2) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800E64B0: queues an 0xFA command carrying three byte fields; which channel setting it drives is not established
+void AudioThread_SetChannelIo(s32 arg0, s32 arg1, s32 arg2) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(((arg0 & 0xFF) << 0x10) | 0xFA000000 | ((arg1 & 0xFF) << 8) | (arg2 & 0xFF), 1);
 }
 
